{
  "id": "Compound::DB00155 - Gene::51702",
  "verbalization": "L-citrulline is implicated in the regulation of Protein-arginine Deiminase Activity through its interaction with multiple Padi proteins, namely Padi1, Padi6, and Padi4. These proteins participate in the same biological process, which is central to the deamination of arginine residues. The shared involvement of these Padi proteins in the same activity suggests a functional link between L-citrulline and the overall regulation of this enzymatic pathway. The evidence from the three paths indicates that L-citrulline binds to different Padi proteins, which in turn participate in the same enzymatic activity, ultimately leading to the involvement of Padi3. This suggests that L-citrulline may influence the activity of Padi3 through its interaction with other Padi proteins, potentially modulating the deamination process. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of L-citrulline in the broader context of arginine metabolism and its potential impact on the activity of Padi3.",
